WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:05.310
An oiled-up interview with a childhood crush,
stowing away in a stranger’s trunk and wrestling

00:00:05.310 --> 00:00:07.616
a judo champion at a fancy party.

00:00:07.616 --> 00:00:13.410
Over the years the shameless Impractical Jokers
have come up with some truly unforgettable gags.

00:00:13.410 --> 00:00:18.470
For Murr's punishment for losing "In Poor
Taste Buds", he got what initially seems like

00:00:18.470 --> 00:00:23.390
a pretty enjoyable task: being a culinary
expert and critic tasting and rating food

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:24.680
in front of a class.

00:00:24.680 --> 00:00:29.500
However, the guys soon let him in on the twist:
his mouth is going to be injected with as

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:34.070
much Novocaine as is clinically allowed just
before going on stage, meaning he won't be

00:00:34.070 --> 00:00:36.710
able to taste anything or speak properly.

00:00:36.710 --> 00:00:40.960
As soon as the dentist injects the Novocaine,
its effect is noticeable on Murr.

00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:43.710
“I know most people get spaghetti and meatballs
in a bolognese sauce.

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:48.580
Most people get spaghetti and meatballs in
a bolognese sauce.”

00:00:48.580 --> 00:00:54.150
He struggles to pronounce most words, especially
those with the letters ‘b’, ‘p’, ‘s’,

00:00:54.150 --> 00:00:55.150
and ‘f’.

00:00:55.150 --> 00:00:59.190
Taking advantage of this, the guys make him
repeat alliterated sentences using those letters

00:00:59.190 --> 00:01:00.000
constantly.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:01.190
“Braised beef."

00:01:01.190 --> 00:01:02.190
"Is brilliant."

00:01:02.190 --> 00:01:03.660
"Is…

00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:05.119
Braised pffft.

00:01:05.119 --> 00:01:07.550
Braised beef is pfftt.”

00:01:07.550 --> 00:01:12.220
Soon, Murr has to start eating and drinking
the food, which becomes quite the ordeal,

00:01:12.220 --> 00:01:14.960
since he can't feel anything that his mouth
is doing.

00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:19.130
The combination of Murr's hilarious struggles
with completing sentences, along with the

00:01:19.130 --> 00:01:24.050
great audience reaction, make "In Poor Taste
Buds" one of Murr's top pranks of all time.

00:01:24.530 --> 00:01:28.820
The guys in "Impractical Jokers" kick off
Season 2 with a bang with the episode "Elephant

00:01:28.820 --> 00:01:29.526
in the Room."

00:01:29.526 --> 00:01:34.010
The first challenge is the "Holy Molar" challenge,
which sees the guys pretending to be dentists

00:01:34.010 --> 00:01:37.689
and interacting with patients, of course having
to do whatever they are told.

00:01:37.689 --> 00:01:42.439
For example, Q informs his patient he has
an embarrassing story about sexually transmitted

00:01:42.439 --> 00:01:46.400
infections and Atlantic City before using
the suction wand on his face.

00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:49.630
“Tell him that's not your worst story about
crabs."

00:01:49.630 --> 00:01:54.620
"That's not my worst story involving crab
in Atlantic City if you know what I mean.”

00:01:54.620 --> 00:01:59.500
Sal's up next, and he has to practically invert
his patient on the dental chair before running

00:01:59.500 --> 00:02:02.880
out of the room and leaving him hanging upside
down for several minutes.

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:05.790
“Keep the chair moving the whole time buddy.

00:02:05.790 --> 00:02:06.790
Don't stop.”

00:02:06.790 --> 00:02:10.619
Joe starts telling his patient about the various
dental tools at his disposal, including shoe

00:02:10.619 --> 00:02:12.730
horns and dubiously named pliers.

00:02:12.730 --> 00:02:17.480
“In the industry, we call this the bi-lateral
hammer ray rammer.”

00:02:17.480 --> 00:02:22.851
The best performance is from Murr, who simply
spins and twirls around the room on the wheeled chair.

00:02:22.851 --> 00:02:27.230
For the "Strip High Five" prank, Murr and
Joe have to deal with an ultra-rare double

00:02:27.230 --> 00:02:31.530
punishment when both of them tie for last
after three challenges.

00:02:31.530 --> 00:02:35.480
The two have to stand in the middle of Union
Square and play a game of strip high five.

00:02:35.480 --> 00:02:39.390
The idea is that each of them has to try and
get strangers to high-five them.

00:02:39.390 --> 00:02:44.060
For every stranger who refuses to high-five
them, they have to remove an article of clothing.

00:02:44.060 --> 00:02:48.390
Both of the guys have some success at first,
as most people are pretty friendly.

00:02:48.390 --> 00:02:52.230
As soon as they start losing more clothes,
people are more reluctant to have anything

00:02:52.230 --> 00:02:54.980
to do with them.

00:02:54.980 --> 00:02:56.720
“Sir high-five."

00:02:56.720 --> 00:02:57.720
"Nope?

00:02:57.720 --> 00:02:58.720
F–k!”

00:02:58.720 --> 00:03:02.620
Pretty soon, the guys attract a crowd of onlookers,
and they both get down to their underwear.

00:03:02.620 --> 00:03:06.970
Joe is successful in getting a high five in
his underwear, but Murr is not so lucky.

00:03:06.970 --> 00:03:08.206
“Please give me a high five.

00:03:08.206 --> 00:03:09.286
Oh no!

00:03:09.286 --> 00:03:10.286
Please.

00:03:10.286 --> 00:03:11.286
Yeah!

00:03:11.286 --> 00:03:12.128
Yeah!

00:03:12.128 --> 00:03:13.128
Yeah!

00:03:13.128 --> 00:03:14.128
Yeah!”

00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:19.060
And he ends up getting his underwear pulled
down by Joe in the middle of the street.

00:03:19.060 --> 00:03:22.690
Joe then grabs the rest of Murr's clothes
and dashes off, leaving him standing there

00:03:22.690 --> 00:03:26.030
barely able to cover himself, looking deeply,
deeply ashamed.

00:03:26.030 --> 00:03:28.100
It was, as Q called it,

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:29.736
“The most public of humiliations”

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:34.260
Season 1 of "Impractical Jokers" has some
of the series' best moments, and the "That

00:03:34.260 --> 00:03:35.260
Looks Delicious!"

00:03:35.260 --> 00:03:38.760
prank from the episode titled "Out of TP"
is no exception.

00:03:38.760 --> 00:03:42.260
For this challenge, the guys find themselves
at a buffet restaurant.

00:03:42.260 --> 00:03:45.830
Unfortunately for them, they aren't allowed
to purchase any of the food.

00:03:45.830 --> 00:03:50.730
Instead, they have to grab food from the plates
of unsuspecting diners, and whoever ends with

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:53.260
the least amount of food on their plate loses.

00:03:53.260 --> 00:03:57.873
Q goes first, but he almost immediately forfeits
after no one gives him the time of day.

00:03:57.873 --> 00:03:58.873
“Hi.

00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:00.299
How are you?

00:04:00.299 --> 00:04:01.415
You seem very nice.

00:04:01.415 --> 00:04:01.915
I’m not.

00:04:01.915 --> 00:04:02.915
Okay.”

00:04:04.222 --> 00:04:08.840
Murr gets caught instantly trying to grab
some corn, and another guy notices him grabbing

00:04:08.840 --> 00:04:10.819
a wing, though he doesn't say anything.

00:04:10.819 --> 00:04:15.349
He steals another woman's okra, and his plate
ends up weighing a respectable 1 lb, 4 oz

00:04:15.349 --> 00:04:16.349
at the end.

00:04:16.349 --> 00:04:19.699
Sal immediately starts grabbing food from
patrons left and right, but he only comes

00:04:19.699 --> 00:04:21.200
up with 1 lb total.

00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:23.150
“The amount of dirty looks that are getting
thrown your way.

00:04:23.150 --> 00:04:25.380
There’s mayhem going on out here.

00:04:25.380 --> 00:04:28.940
This is complete mayhem.”

00:04:28.940 --> 00:04:34.430
Joe is the final contestant, and he starts
scatting while grabbing food from a few female patrons.

00:04:34.430 --> 00:04:38.389
One of them alerts her husband, who decides
to test Joe out and see if he tries it with him.

00:04:38.389 --> 00:04:41.600
When Joe does, the guy smacks his macaroni
spoon away from him.

00:04:41.600 --> 00:04:45.660
Joe ends up following him to the table and
grabs some fried chicken after a brief tong

00:04:45.660 --> 00:04:49.560
fight, but his plate still weighs under a
pound and he loses along with Q.

00:04:49.836 --> 00:04:54.180
The best "Impractical Jokers" punishments
are brutally public, and the one from "Below

00:04:54.180 --> 00:04:56.410
the Belt" is an all-time classic.

00:04:56.410 --> 00:04:59.690
Murr is the loser of the episode, so he has
to endure the punishment.

00:04:59.690 --> 00:05:04.280
His task is to deliver a PowerPoint lecture
on the science behind climate change, which

00:05:04.280 --> 00:05:06.440
Murr claims he can do in his sleep.

00:05:06.440 --> 00:05:10.350
However, while Murr is giving the speech,
the guys will have access to his lower body

00:05:10.350 --> 00:05:13.120
via a hollow table he is standing in front
of.

00:05:13.120 --> 00:05:16.370
The audience can't see the guys under the
table, and they immediately start making Murr's

00:05:16.370 --> 00:05:18.880
presentation as difficult as possible.

00:05:18.880 --> 00:05:24.520
Sal begins by waxing one of Murr's legs while
he's speaking, making Murr grimace and squirm.

00:05:24.520 --> 00:05:26.819
“Still allows.

00:05:26.819 --> 00:05:27.970
AHA!"

00:05:27.970 --> 00:05:31.650
Next up is Q, who sprays Murr's pants with
a water bottle to make it look like he wet

00:05:31.650 --> 00:05:32.650
himself.

00:05:32.650 --> 00:05:36.280
He then has to step on a mouse trap and walk
around wearing high-heeled shoes, confusing

00:05:36.280 --> 00:05:37.940
the audience immensely.

00:05:37.940 --> 00:05:43.210
But that wasn’t even the most embarrassing
part of the prank.

00:05:43.210 --> 00:05:45.910
“What?

00:05:45.910 --> 00:05:48.620
"Hi."

00:05:48.620 --> 00:05:52.560
The coup de grace is when Joe turns Murr's
slacks into short shorts, again making him

00:05:52.560 --> 00:05:55.968
parade around in front of a bewildered and
amused audience.

00:05:55.968 --> 00:06:00.630
As punishment for losing the "Junk in the
Trunk" challenges, Sal had one of his most

00:06:00.630 --> 00:06:02.810
high-energy moments on the show.

00:06:02.810 --> 00:06:06.789
The gag is that the guys are at a local car
rental agency and Sal has to hide in the trunk

00:06:06.789 --> 00:06:08.230
of one of the vehicles.

00:06:08.230 --> 00:06:11.900
He's supposed to ride along in the trunk until
the person needs to open it, at which point

00:06:11.900 --> 00:06:13.780
they'll see him and be shocked.

00:06:13.780 --> 00:06:17.949
The prank gets off to a seemingly rocky start
when the renters take the car on a much longer

00:06:17.949 --> 00:06:19.479
trip than expected.

00:06:19.479 --> 00:06:24.680
Sal rattles around in the trunk while the
woman drives around, smacking his head several times.

00:06:24.680 --> 00:06:26.420
“I just went flying.

00:06:26.420 --> 00:06:27.420
Ohh.

00:06:27.850 --> 00:06:29.568
Speed bumps coming up.

00:06:29.568 --> 00:06:32.738
Oh god no no no.”

00:06:33.190 --> 00:06:38.190
Eventually, the car stops, and a woman gets
out and opens the trunk.

00:06:38.190 --> 00:06:43.870
“Hi, I’m sorry.”

00:06:43.870 --> 00:06:49.030
Finally, when it seems like the woman is truly
upset, Joe reveals the truth: It's actually

00:06:49.030 --> 00:06:52.370
his friend Melissa, who knew about Sal in
the trunk the whole time.

00:06:52.370 --> 00:06:56.160
Her getting upset was all an act and Sal bought
it, hook, line, and sinker.

00:06:56.160 --> 00:06:57.160
“Where are we?

00:06:57.160 --> 00:06:58.160
Around the corner.

00:06:58.160 --> 00:06:59.160
Yeah, we like went around the corner.

00:06:59.160 --> 00:07:00.713
Just went around the block.

00:07:00.849 --> 00:07:01.849
Oh god.”

00:07:01.967 --> 00:07:06.910
One of the funniest recurring pranks on "Impractical
Jokers" is the "Did I Deserve That?"

00:07:06.910 --> 00:07:07.910
challenge.

00:07:07.910 --> 00:07:11.349
For these challenges, the guys are working
as cashiers behind a store counter when an

00:07:11.349 --> 00:07:15.060
irate customer barges in and throws water
at their faces while they are in the middle

00:07:15.060 --> 00:07:16.349
of a transaction.

00:07:16.349 --> 00:07:20.510
The guys then have to sell whatever excuse
they are told to get the customer to say they

00:07:20.510 --> 00:07:21.690
did not deserve it.

00:07:21.690 --> 00:07:22.700
“What did we do wrong?

00:07:22.700 --> 00:07:24.009
We’re gonna find out!

00:07:24.009 --> 00:07:26.669
And no matter how bad it is, we’ve gotta
defend it.”

00:07:26.669 --> 00:07:29.930
The first time the guys did the challenge
was during the episode "The Blunder Years",

00:07:29.930 --> 00:07:32.000
and it was one of the funniest of the series.

00:07:32.000 --> 00:07:34.490
Joe and Sal successfully get a "no" from their
customers.

00:07:34.490 --> 00:07:37.790
“I put like thousands of mosquitos in his
house and I thought he’d like get the hint.

00:07:37.790 --> 00:07:39.889
I mean do you think I deserved that?

00:07:39.889 --> 00:07:40.889
"No.”

00:07:40.889 --> 00:07:45.210
But Murr doesn't have the same luck, though
he does win $100 in a side bet from Joe after

00:07:45.210 --> 00:07:47.470
caressing the chest hair of a customer.

00:07:47.470 --> 00:07:52.020
The final participant is Q, but that's when
the entire prank goes awry and ends up creating

00:07:52.020 --> 00:07:54.451
one of the best "Impractical Jokers" moments
of all time.

00:07:54.451 --> 00:07:55.451
“Oh my god!

00:07:55.451 --> 00:08:03.220
He threw it at the wrong guy!"

00:08:03.220 --> 00:08:07.900
The actor quickly realizes his mistake but
maintains there's nothing he can do now.

00:08:07.900 --> 00:08:11.730
Luckily, the aggrieved party is a good sport
about the whole thing and is able to laugh

00:08:11.730 --> 00:08:12.730
it off.

00:08:12.871 --> 00:08:16.532
You know the punishment is going to be good
in "Impractical Jokers" when it covers almost

00:08:16.532 --> 00:08:17.970
half the episode.

00:08:17.970 --> 00:08:22.560
And Murr's Judo bout during a poolside cocktail
party in the episode "The Party Crasher" is

00:08:22.560 --> 00:08:24.289
one of these rare few.

00:08:24.289 --> 00:08:29.000
For this punishment, Murr has to crash a cocktail
party and start a wrestling match with two-time

00:08:29.000 --> 00:08:32.849
U.S. Olympic Gold Medalist Judo champion Kayla
Harrison.

00:08:32.849 --> 00:08:38.019
Murr already looks incredibly conspicuous
wearing a wig made from Q's hair and his constant

00:08:38.019 --> 00:08:41.490
flailing at Kayla quickly gets the attention
of all of the party guests.

00:08:41.490 --> 00:08:44.830
And he’s only allowed to say one thing about
the situation.

00:08:44.830 --> 00:08:47.990
“I know her from college.”

00:08:47.990 --> 00:08:53.209
After she rips off his toupee during an ill-fated
takedown attempt, he has to put it back on

00:08:53.209 --> 00:08:56.310
and continue wearing it, looking completely
disheveled.

00:08:56.310 --> 00:09:00.570
At one point, Kayla throws Murr through a
table, and he just tries to play it off as

00:09:00.570 --> 00:09:06.510
best he can.

00:09:06.510 --> 00:09:11.910
For the finale, Kayla launches Murr over her
head into the pool after his final failed attack.

00:09:11.910 --> 00:09:16.019
The guests clap and cheer for Kayla, who walks
back and enjoys the rest of the party.

00:09:16.019 --> 00:09:20.260
Seeing Murr get manhandled by an Olympic Gold
Medalist was a highlight of the season and

00:09:20.260 --> 00:09:23.246
one of the best celebrity cameos of the entire
series.

00:09:23.409 --> 00:09:27.510
The episode "Blind Justice" features one of
Sal's best all-time punishments.

00:09:27.510 --> 00:09:32.460
His task is to act as a hardened convict and
give a scared-straight speech to a room full

00:09:32.460 --> 00:09:33.460
of teenagers.

00:09:33.460 --> 00:09:38.090
He thinks the only catch is that he has to
wear a pair of sunglasses that 100% obscure

00:09:38.090 --> 00:09:40.620
his view and use a few props.

00:09:40.620 --> 00:09:44.839
However, the guys reveal to the audience the
true deviousness of the punishment: he is

00:09:44.839 --> 00:09:47.630
in fact, not speaking to a crowd of teenagers.

00:09:47.630 --> 00:09:50.050
"Shut up!

00:09:50.050 --> 00:09:53.510
I don’t wanna hear anybody."

00:09:53.510 --> 00:09:57.180
He lectures them about not disappointing their
parents and warns them about spending the

00:09:57.180 --> 00:09:59.540
next 50 years of their life in prison.

00:09:59.540 --> 00:10:02.020
The audience starts laughing at the ridiculous
speech.

00:10:02.020 --> 00:10:06.010
Sal hears this but doesn't fully understand,
which just makes him yell more.

00:10:06.010 --> 00:10:07.210
“You look nice and tight boy!

00:10:07.210 --> 00:10:10.870
That’s what people are gonna tell you in
there."

00:10:10.870 --> 00:10:12.820
Eventually, he puts two and two together.

00:10:12.820 --> 00:10:15.870
“This is so not teens.

00:10:15.870 --> 00:10:19.160
Take the glasses off.

00:10:19.160 --> 00:10:20.160
Oh.”

00:10:20.160 --> 00:10:25.209
And for the grand finale, Sal shows them his
Jaden Smith tattoo, which makes them all break

00:10:25.209 --> 00:10:26.910
out in hysterics.

00:10:27.053 --> 00:10:31.910
It's no secret to fans of the show that Murr
had a massive childhood crush on Danica McKellar,

00:10:31.910 --> 00:10:34.769
an actress from one of his favorite childhood
shows "The Wonder Years."

00:10:34.769 --> 00:10:38.750
For his punishment in the "The Blunder Years"
episode, Murr has to interview McKellar in

00:10:38.750 --> 00:10:40.639
a hotel conference room.

00:10:40.639 --> 00:10:44.980
While that sounds pretty desirable, Murr has
to do so while completely oiled up and wearing

00:10:44.980 --> 00:10:46.190
a speedo.

00:10:46.190 --> 00:10:50.820
The guys tell him he's going to enter a bodybuilding
contest, which gives them cover to douse him

00:10:50.820 --> 00:10:53.480
with oil and put him in a speedo, but it was
all just a ruse.

00:10:53.480 --> 00:10:59.620
“Behind the door is gonna be a celebrity
that is Murray’s childhood crush.”

00:10:59.620 --> 00:11:01.640
During the interview, Murr is told what to
say.

00:11:01.640 --> 00:11:03.380
“Truth or dare?

00:11:03.380 --> 00:11:05.120
I’ll go first.

00:11:05.120 --> 00:11:06.120
Truth.

00:11:06.120 --> 00:11:08.700
I used to kiss a poster of you when I was
younger.”

00:11:08.700 --> 00:11:13.510
And she is told to act as harshly as possible
with Murr and she delivers in spades.

00:11:13.510 --> 00:11:16.269
“Finish this equation.

00:11:16.269 --> 00:11:19.220
Me plus you equals.

00:11:19.220 --> 00:11:23.209
"Really awkward.”

00:11:23.209 --> 00:11:28.050
After thoroughly embarrassing himself by trying
to do squats and flex for her, Murr is mercifully

00:11:28.050 --> 00:11:30.070
allowed to leave the room and McKellar alone.

00:11:30.070 --> 00:11:34.870
As soon as he walks out, she bursts out laughing,
but Murr is probably scarred for life.

00:11:35.395 --> 00:11:40.430
The pranks where the guys participate in panels
are definite staples on "Impractical Jokers."

00:11:40.430 --> 00:11:43.620
One of Q's most hilarious was from "Brother
of the Sisterhood".

00:11:43.620 --> 00:11:47.899
Q has to sit in on a panel of experts talking
about feminism, posing as the author of a

00:11:47.899 --> 00:11:49.980
blog titled "Brother of the Sisterhood."

00:11:49.980 --> 00:11:53.139
And of course, he must disagree with everything
the panelists say.

00:11:53.139 --> 00:11:55.220
“I think Michelle Obama’s a fantastic
example.

00:11:55.220 --> 00:11:56.220
Right.

00:11:56.220 --> 00:11:59.760
But she wouldn’t be in the White House if
her husband hadn’t gotten there.”

00:11:59.760 --> 00:12:04.080
The host is in on the joke, but no one else
is, least of all the audience members.

00:12:04.080 --> 00:12:08.149
First, Q has to explain the difference between
"men's jobs" and "women's jobs.”

00:12:08.149 --> 00:12:09.149
“Hey man.

00:12:09.149 --> 00:12:10.149
You know I’m all for women’s rights.

00:12:10.149 --> 00:12:13.160
I mean who isn’t, but I also want my car
to run well.”

00:12:13.160 --> 00:12:17.430
Then he is forced to defend a quote from his
fictional blog where he claimed that women

00:12:17.430 --> 00:12:20.950
becoming mothers turn "emotionally unstable
and irrational."

00:12:20.950 --> 00:12:25.740
“These ladies, they’re going through a
lot.

00:12:25.740 --> 00:12:27.480
You know."

00:12:27.480 --> 00:12:29.209
"Great answer.”

00:12:29.209 --> 00:12:34.120
After several minutes of excruciatingly uncomfortable
and cringeworthy banter, Q has to give his

00:12:34.120 --> 00:12:35.980
closing remarks.

00:12:35.980 --> 00:12:40.139
And they consist solely of him telling the
almost exclusively female audience that he

00:12:40.139 --> 00:12:43.970
finds it amazing they can go all day without
playing with their breasts.

00:12:43.970 --> 00:12:49.839
It is without a doubt one of Q's most embarrassing
and awkward punishments in the series.

00:12:49.839 --> 00:12:54.990
"The Q-Pay" might be the best-known and longest-lasting
prank in "Impractical Jokers" history.

00:12:54.990 --> 00:12:59.430
Murr's the loser in this episode and his punishment
is that he has to wear a wig.

00:12:59.430 --> 00:13:03.560
It doesn't sound too bad until you realize
whose hair he's wearing: Q's.

00:13:03.560 --> 00:13:08.000
The guys have Q cut off his shoulder-length
hair and make it into a wig for Murray.

00:13:08.000 --> 00:13:09.000
“Oh my god."

00:13:09.000 --> 00:13:10.000
"No!

00:13:10.000 --> 00:13:11.000
No!"

00:13:11.000 --> 00:13:15.040
"That hair is going on that head.”

00:13:15.040 --> 00:13:18.800
The wig doesn't look half bad at first but
doesn't suit Murr at all.

00:13:18.800 --> 00:13:22.880
To make matters worse, Murr has to get his
passport picture taken with the wig.

00:13:22.880 --> 00:13:27.140
This is to contrast with Murr's driver's license,
which features him with a shaved head and

00:13:27.140 --> 00:13:29.709
shaved eyebrows from an earlier punishment.

00:13:29.709 --> 00:13:32.000
Murr claims the hair smells like:

00:13:32.000 --> 00:13:35.250
“Whiskey and pot.”

00:13:35.250 --> 00:13:39.130
Unfortunately for Murr, he can't just take
off the wig after a day; he has to keep it

00:13:39.130 --> 00:13:41.079
on for the remainder of the season.

00:13:41.079 --> 00:13:45.290
There are several more episodes in Season
6 after "The Q-Pay," and Murr's hair just

00:13:45.290 --> 00:13:47.640
gets worse and worse as time goes on.

00:13:47.640 --> 00:13:51.520
The fact that it keeps going throughout the
season makes it by far the best "Impractical

00:13:51.520 --> 00:13:53.350
Jokers" prank in the series.

00:13:53.350 --> 00:13:57.339
It's almost like multiple punishments in one,
as every episode with him wearing it is like

00:13:57.339 --> 00:13:58.190
an extra prank.

